})();</script></div></div></div><div class="KLEmSd"></div><div data-encoded-docid="mrjoMgYqiH2JAGQKAAAAAA==" data-implicit-notification-eligible="false" data-result-index="0" data-title="Data Analyst-Associate" role="group" jscontroller="leJiCf" jsdata="ZSBYQe;_;kvn4aunMNpCe4-EP6dygqAQ61 xQKg9c;_;kvn4aunMNpCe4-EP6dygqAQ63" jsaction="rcuQ6b:npT2md"><div><div class="XFOJCe"><h2 class="HKvozf IFnjPb">Job description</h2><span jsname="QAWWu" class="OOyDTc">Minimum Degree Required (BQ) *: Bachelors Degree<br><br>Degree Preferred: Bachelors Degree<br><br>Required Field(s) of Study (BQ): Computer Science, Information Technology, Data Analytics, Data Engineering<br><br>Preferred Field(s) of Study: Cloud Computing, Software Engineering<br><br>Minimum Year(s) of Experience (BQ) *: 4+ years of experience<br><br>Certification(s) Preferred:<br>• Databricks Certified Data Analyst Associate<br>•</span><span jsname="pqRzIf">...</span><span jsname="ij8cu" class="ejCXj" id="tsuid_kvn4aunMNpCe4-EP6dygqAQ_186" aria-live="polite" style="display:none">&#160;Databricks Certified Data Engineer Associate<br>• AWS Certified Cloud Practitioner<br>• Microsoft Power BI Data Analyst c ertification (PL-300).<br>• Certifications are preferred, not required; hands-on experience carries more weight.<br><br>Required Knowledge/Skills (BQ):<br>• Strong SQL: joins, subqueries, CTEs, window functions, aggregations, and query optimization, on SQL Server or another relational database.<br>• Ability to build and maintain database objects such as tables, views, indexes, and stored procedures.<br>• Hands-on Databricks experience: notebooks, Spark SQL, Delta tables, and building datasets in Bronze, Silver, and Gold layers; working knowledge of PySpark.<br>• Python (pandas, PySpark) for data transformation, validation, and automation.<br>• Working knowledge of AWS for data: Amazon S3 for storage and IAM basics, with exposure to Athena, Glue, or Redshift.<br>• Experience extracting and transforming large datasets using SQL-based processing and ETL/ELT techniques, including incremental loads.<br>• Experience developing operational reports and dashboards in Power BI or Tableau; advanced Excel including pivot tables and formulas.<br>• Experience performing data validation, reconciliation, and troubleshooting data discrepancies.<br>• Strong understanding of data modeling and analytics dataset design (fact and dimension tables, star schemas).<br>• Ability to analyze large datasets and identify trends, patterns, and operational insights.<br>• Awareness of HIPAA and PHI handling, and strong analytical thinking and problem-solving skills.<br><br>Preferred Knowledge/Skills *:<br>• Databricks Workflows, Unity Catalog, Auto Loader, and Databricks SQL dashboards.<br>• AWS Glue (jobs and Data Catalog), Athena, Lambda, and CloudWatch.<br>• Azure Data Factory and ADLS Gen2, since some engagements run on Azure.<br>• Experience building or supporting ETL/ELT pipelines, and migrating SQL Server logic to a lakehouse.<br>• Exposure to Alteryx, Informatica, or similar ETL tools.<br>• Git and basic CI/CD for data code.<br>• Microsoft Power Platform (Power Apps, Power Automate) for workflow automation.<br>• Experience with healthcare datasets or Revenue Cycle Management (RCM) environments, including EDI X12 835/837. Healthcare experience is not mandatory.<br><br>QUALIFICATIONS: Education / Experience:<br>• BE/BTECH, ME/MTECH, MBA, BCA/MCA, or a related field, or an equivalent amount of relevant professional experience.<br>• 4+ years of experience in data analytics, data engineering, or reporting roles.<br>• Hands-on experience with SQL databases and with Databricks (Spark SQL, Delta tables).<br>• Working experience with Python and with AWS data storage such as Amazon S3.<br>• Experience building dashboards, analytics datasets, and operational reports in Power BI or Tableau.<br>• Experience with ETL pipelines or data transformation workflows.<br>• Experience working with large operational dataset