g knowledge of PySpark.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003ePython (pandas, PySpark) for data transformation, validation, and automation.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eWorking knowledge of AWS for data: Amazon S3 for storage and IAM basics, with exposure to Athena, Glue, or Redshift.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eExperience extracting and transforming large datasets using SQL-based processing and ETL/ELT techniques, including incremental loads.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eExperience developing operational reports and dashboards in Power BI or Tableau; advanced Excel including pivot tables and formulas.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eExperience performing data validation, reconciliation, and troubleshooting data discrepancies.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eStrong understanding of data modeling and analytics dataset design (fact and dimension tables, star schemas).\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eAbility to analyze large datasets and identify trends, patterns, and operational insights.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eAwareness of HIPAA and PHI handling, and strong analytical thinking and problem-solving skills.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cb\u003ePreferred Knowledge/Skills *:\u003c/b\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eDatabricks Workflows, Unity Catalog, Auto Loader, and Databricks SQL dashboards.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eAWS Glue (jobs and Data Catalog), Athena, Lambda, and CloudWatch.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eAzure Data Factory and ADLS Gen2, since some engagements run on Azure.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eExperience building or supporting ETL/ELT pipelines, and migrating SQL Server logic to a lakehouse.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eExposure to Alteryx, Informatica, or similar ETL tools.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eGit and basic CI/CD for data code.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eMicrosoft Power Platform (Power Apps, Power Automate) for workflow automation.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eExperience with healthcare datasets or Revenue Cycle Management (RCM) environments, including EDI X12 835/837. Healthcare experience is not mandatory.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cb\u003eQUALIFICATIONS: Education / Experience:\u003c/b\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eBE/BTECH, ME/MTECH, MBA, BCA/MCA, or a related field, or an equivalent amount of relevant professional experience.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e4+ years of experience in data analytics, data engineering, or reporting roles.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eHands-on experience with SQL databases and with Databricks (Spark SQL, Delta tables).\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eWorking experience with Python and with AWS data storage such as Amazon S3.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eExperience building dashboards, analytics datasets, and operational reports in Power BI or Tableau.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eExperience with ETL pipelines or data transformation workflows.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eExperience working with large operational datasets, including validation and reconciliation.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eExperience working in healthcare, insurance, or regulated industries is preferred.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cb\u003eAdditional Information:\u003c/b\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eShift timings: Flexible to work in night shifts (US Time zone)\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eExperience Level: 3–5 years\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eMode of working: Work from office\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eLine of Service: Advisory\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eDesignation: Associate\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eRole: Data Analyst (Databricks, SQL \u0026 AWS)\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eLocation: Bangalore\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003ePrimary Technology Stack: SQL Server, Databricks (Spark SQL, PySpark, Delta Lake), Python, AWS (S3, IAM), Power BI, Excel\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003ePreferred Technologies: Databricks Workflows / Unity Catalog / Auto Loader, AWS Glue / Athena / Lambda, Azure Data Factory, Tableau, Alteryx / Informatica, Gi